Problem Recap

We are designing an Elevator System with:
Multiple floors (e.g., 50)
Multiple elevators (e.g., 6)
Each elevator has its own controller.
A centralized Scheduler/Dispatcher decides which elevator serves a request.

Entities:
Elevator System
ElevatorCar
Floor
Door
Display
Request
Schedular

methods:
assignElevator()
moveToFloor
openDoor()
closeDoor()
clearTarget()

Data flow:
User -> ElevatorSystemController().requestElevator()
             -> creates Floor Request
             -> ElevatorController.handleRequest()
             -> Schedular.assignElevator()
             -> ElevatorCar.addRequest() + move()
             -> Door open/close
             -> Request served -> Elevator IDLE


Design Patterns:
Singleton → ElevatorSystem
Strategy → SchedulerAlgorithm
State → ElevatorCar state transitions
Observer → FloorButton notifications



